-- title:
--   An f-stable cyclic subgroup of order M from a split quadratic relation
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an additive commutative group and let $M$ be a natural number with $M \neq 0$. Suppose given an isomorphism of additive groups $e \colon \mathbb{Z}/M \times \mathbb{Z}/M \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \{x \in G : M x = 0\}$, where the target is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $G$ of elements annihilated by the integer $M$. Suppose further given an additive endomorphism $f \colon G \to G$ and integers $u, v$ with $M \mid uv - 1$, such that for every $x \in G$ with $M x = 0$ one has $f(f(x)) = u\, f(x)$. Then there exists an additive subgroup $C \le G$ which is cyclic (i.e. generated by a single element), whose cardinality as a natural number is $M$, and which satisfies $f(x) \in C$ for all $x \in C$. Note that the hypothesis on $f$ is imposed only on the $M$-torsion, the conclusion asserts stability $f(C) \subseteq C$ rather than any compatibility of $f$ with a generator, and no assertion is made that $C$ lies in the $M$-torsion (although the generator produced has additive order $M$).
--
--   This is the elementary group-theoretic mechanism producing a $\Gamma_0(M)$-type level structure (a cyclic subgroup of order $M$) stable under a given endomorphism, from the fact that on the $M$-torsion $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^2$ the endomorphism satisfies a quadratic relation splitting with the two roots $0$ and $u$, the latter invertible modulo $M$. It is used in the construction underlying [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_supersingular_endomorphism_natCard_ker_eq_odd_pow_stabilizing_cyclic`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_supersingular_endomorphism_natCard_ker_eq_odd_pow_stabilizing_cyclic), where $G$ is the group of points of an elliptic curve.
